From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:07:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Decode PT 121 (mlow-red) audio by its SplitRed main frame

Seen live: a member left a group call and joined it again; the others then
sent it PT 121 (MLow with SplitRed redundancy) instead of PT 120. The packets
authenticated (2 failures in 875) and produced frames, but every frame was
silent: the receiver accepted PT 121 yet decoded the RED payload as a bare
MLow frame, reading the redundancy header as the frame's TOC. The member
heard nobody while everyone heard it.

The RTP payload type now travels with each authenticated audio packet to
the decoder; PT 121 is unpacked with DepackSplitRed and its main frame
decoded, an unpackable one concealed. PT 120 is unchanged.

Tested: a PT 121 stream decodes sample for sample like the same frames sent
bare, and is not silent; a broken RED payload is concealed for a full frame;
full suite passes.
